{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>בן פורת יוסף</b> He did not mention him by name as he did for the others, for he honored him on account of the kingship, and began with the name of his sons. בן פורת in gematria: מנשה ואפרים. Another interpretation: בן פורת — בן פותר, on account of the interpretation of dreams:" "<b>בנות צעדה עלי שור</b> He prophesied concerning Joshua's war against Jericho, that they would shoot arrows at him from the wall:"], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The phrase 'בן פורת בן פותר' is a notarikon/wordplay: 'a son of porat' read as 'a son of poter (an interpreter).'"}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:47.747521165Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}